{"id":"b210b4aec5655f2446616487610703f50cb1eeac","axis":"silent","repo":"elsa-workflows/elsa-core","sha":"b210b4aec5655f2446616487610703f50cb1eeac","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".github/workflows/apps-source-validation.yml","lines":["@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@ on:","       - 'Elsa.Apps.slnf'","       - 'scripts/solution/**'","       - 'scripts/integration-program/verify_apps_source_import.py'","+      - 'scripts/integration-program/apps_consumer_inventory.py'","       - 'scripts/integration-program/test_verify_apps_source_import.py'","       - 'docs/integration-program/apps-source-import.json'","       - '.github/workflows/apps-source-validation.yml'","@@ -68,7 +69,7 @@ jobs:","           python3 scripts/container_release.py validate-run \\","             --event pull_request --publish false --images all \\","             --ref \"$SOURCE_REF\" --commit \"$EXPECTED_HEAD\"","-      - name: Restore and build all nine package consumers","+      - name: Restore and build all current package consumers","         run: |","           dotnet restore Elsa.Apps.slnf --force-evaluate","           dotnet restore apps/ElsaApps.sln","@@ -95,7 +96,7 @@ jobs:","       - name: Verify candidate identity","         run: test \"$(git rev-parse HEAD)\" = \"$EXPECTED_HEAD\"","       - name: Build a local AMD64 image without publication","-        uses: docker/build-push-action@v6","+        uses: docker/build-push-action@10e90e3645eae34f1e60eeb005ba3a3d33f178e8 # v6","         env:","           DOCKER_BUILD_RECORD_UPLOAD: 'false'","           DOCKER_BUILD_SUMMARY: 'false'"],"additions":3,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":".github/workflows/current-import-impact.yml","lines":["@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ on:","       - '.github/**'","       - 'build/**'","       - 'scripts/integration-program/**'","-      - 'docs/integration-program/apps-source-import.json'","+      - 'Elsa.Apps.slnf'","       - 'core/samples/**'","       - 'extensions/samples/**'","       - 'studio/samples/**'"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":".github/workflows/integration-program-tools.yml","lines":["@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@ on:","       - '**/global.json'","       - 'docs/integration-program/consolidation/dependabot-recursive-discovery.md'","       - 'scripts/integration-program/**'","-      - 'docs/integration-program/apps-source-import.json'","+      - 'Elsa.Apps.slnf'","       - 'extensions/src/Elsa.Testing.Extensions/**'","       - 'extensions/samples/workbench/**'","       - 'docs/integration-program/verify-hierarchy.py'"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/integration-program/apps-source-import.md","lines":["@@ -69,22 +69,29 @@ Final acceptance additionally requires fresh author-independent Elsa 3 Code Revi"," ## Maintaining Apps after the source cutoff"," "," The first import commit, original source refs/tree, asset modes/blobs and original","-89-file mapping are historical evidence. Never rewrite them or append new Core-authored","-files as though they came from the original source. For an intentional edit to an","-original mapped file, add its path to `adaptedSourceFiles` in the reviewed change if","-needed, retain its original blob/mode entry, explain the adaptation in the PR, and run","-the affected product and source gates. This exemption records a reviewed content delta;","-it does not waive functional tests. New non-project files belong to normal Core review","-and product validation and do not expand the original import inventory.","-","-The current source-import verifier, Dependabot disposition and source-impact partition","-are deliberately bounded to the original nine project manifests. A tenth project cannot","-be accepted by metadata alone under these checks. Its owning change must first introduce","-or update a separate **current consumer inventory** and reconcile the filter, verifier,","-discovery/impact checks and product CI without changing the immutable original mapping.","-Until that reviewed tooling change lands, project additions fail closed. Changing current","-package versions likewise requires updating the effective-policy expectations and normal","-product tests; it does not alter original source evidence or activate an updater/publisher.","+89-file mapping are immutable historical evidence. Never rewrite them or append new","+Core-authored files as though they came from the donor. `adaptedSourceFiles` describes","+this import's integration delta only; it is not a permanent exemption list for future","+source changes. The verifier checks original blobs against the immutable import commit,","+then checks current tracked Apps files against the current committed checkout, rejecting","+unsafe paths and symlink traversal. Normal reviewed runtime edits do not alter the ledger.","+","+The current consumer inventory comes from tracked `apps/**/*.csproj` files,","+`Elsa.Apps.slnf` and root `Elsa.sln`; all three must agree exactly. When adding or removing","+an Apps project, maintain the root solution and regenerate its filter with the existing","+solution-group tooling in the same change. Keep references within Apps, scoped package","+consumption and nonpackable defaults. Source-impact selection and dependency discovery","+use this current inventory, so ordinary project additions need no historical ledger entry.","+The effective policy checks compare package-family versions with the current declarations","+in `apps/Directory.Packages.props`; reviewed package updates also require the affected","+product tests. They do not activate an updater or publisher.","+","+The consolidated candidate comparison baseline retains its original 225 package identities","+and 124 exclusions, plus the nine initial Apps nonpackable exclusions. Its original hosted","+artifact evidence is unchanged and does not certify the added rows. A future project","+addition/removal must reconcile its current nonpackable exclusion through normal inventory","+review. The existing package-proof CI supplies evaluated inventory; this source import","+neither prepares a release candidate nor changes release authority."," "," ## Deferred operational ownership"," "],"additions":23,"deletions":16,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/integration-program/consolidation/dependabot-recursive-discovery.md","lines":["@@ -98,9 +98,10 @@ version without freezing future updates. It runs when this manifest changes."," "," Task [#8746](https://github.com/elsa-workflows/elsa-core/issues/8746) adds exactly nine"," registered Apps projects to the shared solution as **independent released-package consumers**.","-The [Apps register](../apps-source-import.json) lists their original manifests. They","+The [Apps register](../apps-source-import.json) preserves their original manifests; the current","+`Elsa.Apps.slnf`, tracked Apps projects and root solution must agree. They"," remain outside these five source-package updater batches; the coverage census explicitly","-reconciles all nine rather than dropping them from inventory. Apps keeps its own","+reconciles the current consumer inventory rather than dropping it from inventory. Apps keeps its own"," `apps/Directory.Packages.props`, `apps/NuGet.Config`, internal project references and"," net10.0 target. Its local targets select only that restore config, prevent source-reference"," substitution and set `IsPackable=false`."],"additions":3,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"scripts/integration-program/apps_consumer_inventory.py","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,74 @@","+\"\"\"Current Apps inventory and checkout safety, independent of the historical import.\"\"\"","+","+import json","+import os","+from pathlib import Path, PurePosixPath","+import re","+import subprocess","+import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET","+","+","+def require(condition: bool, message: object) -> None:","+    if not condition:","+        raise ValueError(str(message))","+","+","+def git_environment() -> dict[str, str]:","+    # Evidence must come from the selected checkout, never ambient repository/config routing.","+    return {key: value for key, value in os.environ.items() if not key.startswith(\"GIT_\")}","+","+","+def git(root: Path, *arguments: str) -> str:","+    return subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), *arguments], cwd=root,","+                                   env=git_environment(), text=True).strip()","+","+","+def regular_file(root: Path, relative: str) -> Path:","+    path = PurePosixPath(relative)","+    require(not path.is_absolute() and \"..\" not in path.parts, f\"Unsafe checkout path: {relative}\")","+    file = root / path","+    for component in (file, *file.parents):","+        if component == root:","+            break","+        require(not component.is_symlink(), f\"Mapped asset traverses a symlink: {relative}\")","+    require(file.resolve().is_relative_to(root), f\"Mapped asset escapes checkout: {relative}\")","+    require(file.is_file(), f\"Missing mapped asset: {relative}\")","+    return file","+","+","+def tracked_apps(root: Path) -> dict[str, tuple[str, str]]:","+    git(root, \"diff\", \"--cached\", \"--quiet\", \"HEAD\", \"--\", \"apps/\")","+    rows = {}","+    for row in git(root, \"ls-files\", \"--stage\", \"-z\", \"--\", \"apps/\").split(\"\\0\"):","+        if not row:","+            continue","+        metadata, path = row.split(\"\\t\", 1)","+        mode, blob, stage = metadata.split()","+        require(stage == \"0\" and mode in {\"100644\", \"100755\"}, f\"Unsafe tracked Apps entry: {path}\")","+        rows[path] = (mode, blob)","+    require(rows, \"Current Apps inventory is empty\")","+    return rows","+","+","+def current_apps_projects(root: Path) -> list[Path]:","+    tracked = {path for path in tracked_apps(root) if path.endswith(\".csproj\")}","+    solution = json.loads(regular_file(root, \"Elsa.Apps.slnf\").read_text())[\"solution\"]","+    require(solution[\"path\"] == \"Elsa.sln\", \"Apps filter must select the root solution\")","+    selected = solution[\"projects\"]","+    require(len(selected) == len(set(selected)) and set(selected) == tracked,","+            \"Apps filter must match every current tracked Apps project exactly once\")","+    root_projects = [path.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\") for path in re.findall(","+        r'\"([^\"\\n]+\\.csproj)\"', regular_file(root, \"Elsa.sln\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\"))]","+    apps_projects = [path for path in root_projects if path.startswith(\"apps/\")]","+    require(len(apps_projects) == len(set(apps_projects)) and set(apps_projects) == tracked,","+            \"Root solution must match the current tracked Apps project inventory\")","+    return [regular_file(root, path) for path in sorted(tracked)]","+","+","+def declared_package_versions(root: Path) -> dict[str, str]:","+    document = ET.parse(regular_file(root, \"apps/Directory.Packages.props\"))","+    versions = {name: document.findtext(f\".//{name}\") for name in","+                (\"ElsaVersion\", \"ElsaStudioVersion\", \"ElsaExtensionsVersion\")}","+    require(all(isinstance(value, str) and value.strip() and \"$(\" not in value","+                for value in versions.values()), \"Apps must declare its current package-family versions\")","+    return versions"],"additions":74,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"scripts/integration-program/consolidated-candidate-inventory-baseline.json","lines":["@@ -628,6 +628,51 @@","       \"id\": \"Elsa.Workflows.Runtime.UnitTests\",","       \"project\": \"test/unit/Elsa.Workflows.Runtime.UnitTests/Elsa.Workflows.Runtime.UnitTests.csproj\",","       \"reason\": \"Project or inherited nonpackable setting remains active\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"id\": \"Elsa.Server.Shared\",","+      \"project\": \"apps/src/Elsa.Server.Shared/Elsa.Server.Shared.csproj\",","+      \"reason\": \"Project or inherited nonpackable setting remains active\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"id\": \"Elsa.Server.Studio.BlazorServer\",","+      \"project\": \"apps/src/Elsa.Server.Studio.BlazorServer/Elsa.Server.Studio.BlazorServer.csproj\",","+      \"reason\": \"Project or inherited nonpackable setting remains active\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"id\": \"Elsa.Server.Studio.BlazorWasm.Client\",","+      \"project\": \"apps/src/Elsa.Server.Studio.BlazorWasm.Client/Elsa.Server.Studio.BlazorWasm.Client.csproj\",","+      \"reason\": \"Project or inherited nonpackable setting remains active\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"id\": \"Elsa.Server.Studio.BlazorWasm\",","+      \"project\": \"apps/src/Elsa.Server.Studio.BlazorWasm/Elsa.Server.Studio.BlazorWasm.csproj\",","+      \"reason\": \"Project or inherited nonpackable setting remains active\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"id\": \"Elsa.Server\",","+      \"project\": \"apps/src/Elsa.Server/Elsa.Server.csproj\",","+      \"reason\": \"Project or inherited nonpackable setting remains active\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"id\": \"Elsa.Studio.BlazorServer\",","+      \"project\": \"apps/src/Elsa.Studio.BlazorServer/Elsa.Studio.BlazorServer.csproj\",","+      \"reason\": \"Project or inherited nonpackable setting remains active\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"id\": \"Elsa.Studio.BlazorWasm.Client\",","+      \"project\": \"apps/src/Elsa.Studio.BlazorWasm.Client/Elsa.Studio.BlazorWasm.Client.csproj\",","+      \"reason\": \"Project or inherited nonpackable setting remains active\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"id\": \"Elsa.Studio.BlazorWasm\",","+      \"project\": \"apps/src/Elsa.Studio.BlazorWasm/Elsa.Studio.BlazorWasm.csproj\",","+      \"reason\": \"Project or inherited nonpackable setting remains active\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"id\": \"Shared\",","+      \"project\": \"apps/src/Shared/Shared.csproj\",","+      \"reason\": \"Project or inherited nonpackable setting remains active\"","     }","   ],","   \"packages\": ["],"additions":45,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"scripts/integration-program/current_import_impact.py","lines":["@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@"," from pathlib import Path"," from typing import Any"," ","+from apps_consumer_inventory import current_apps_projects"," import refresh_canonical_dependency_graph as graph_reader"," from release_unit_manifest import DEFAULT_UNIT_ID, get_unit, load_manifest"," from product_layout import map_path","@@ -41,16 +42,11 @@ def partition_source_graph(","     solution_project_paths: set[str],"," ) -> tuple[dict[str, str], dict[str, dict[str, Any]], dict[str, dict[str, Any]]]:","     \"\"\"Keep registered image consumers outside source-reference impact accounting.\"\"\"","-    register = json.loads((root / \"docs/integration-program/apps-source-import.json\").read_text())","-    registered = [row[\"destinationPath\"] for row in register[\"assets\"]","-                  if row[\"destinationPath\"].endswith(\".csproj\")]","-    independent = set(registered)","-    if (len(registered) != 9 or len(independent) != 9","-            or any(not path.startswith(\"apps/src/\") for path in independent)","-            or {path for path in solution_project_paths if path.startswith(\"apps/\")} != independent","+    independent = {project.relative_to(root).as_posix() for project in current_apps_projects(root)}","+    if ({path for path in solution_project_paths if path.startswith(\"apps/\")} != independent","             or {path for path in project_names if path.startswith(\"apps/\")} != independent","             or not independent.issubset(asset_documents)):","-        raise ValueError(\"Independent Apps inventory must match exactly the nine registered solution projects\")","+        raise ValueError(\"Independent Apps inventory must match current tracked/filter/solution projects\")","     for source, document in asset_documents.items():","         for framework in document[\"project\"][\"restore\"][\"frameworks\"].values():","             for reference_path, reference in framework.get(\"projectReferences\", {}).items():","@@ -252,7 +248,7 @@ def receipt(root: Path, manifest_path: Path, expected_head: str | None) -> dict[","         \"independentPackageConsumers\": {","             \"disposition\": \"Registered Apps image consumers use released packages; excluded from source-reference impact, not claimed as affected-test coverage\",","             \"validationOwner\": \".github/workflows/apps-source-validation.yml\",","-            \"registerSha256\": sha256(root / \"docs/integration-program/apps-source-import.json\"),","+            \"inventoryFilterSha256\": sha256(root / \"Elsa.Apps.slnf\"),","             \"buildConfigSha256\": {path: sha256(root / path)","                                   for path in graph_reader.ancestor_build_configs(root, set(independent_assets))},","             \"projectFileSha256\": {path: sha256(root / path) for path in independent_assets},","@@ -271,7 +267,7 @@ def receipt(root: Path, manifest_path: Path, expected_head: str | None) -> dict[","         \"scenarios\": scenarios,","         \"limitations\": [","             \"Project-reference impact is evaluated from this checkout's restored assets; runtime service effects are not inferred.\",","-            \"Package-type Elsa dependencies in the source-reference graph other than the known package-manifest generator are rejected; the nine registered Apps released-package consumers are separately accounted for and package-to-source edges are not inferred.\",","+            \"Package-type Elsa dependencies in the source-reference graph other than the known package-manifest generator are rejected; the current registered Apps released-package consumers are separately accounted for and package-to-source edges are not inferred.\",","             \"Restored Test SDK projects are selected only when MSBuild evaluates IsTestProject=true for every restored framework.\",","             \"This receipt selects tests but does not execute them or publish packages.\",","             \"The release-unit manifest selects one Slack package; it is not a Core release package plan.\","],"additions":6,"deletions":10,"truncated":false},{"path":"scripts/integration-prog